45 780 Td
(   - Preserving Authorial Anonymity in Blind Peer Review:) Tj
T*
(   - Agentless passives prevent accidental revelation of laboratory identities in double-blind) Tj
T*
(   submission processes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the legitimate role of the active voice in contemporary scientific papers, analyzing guidelines from Nature, Science, and NIH.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Historical Paradigm Shift:) Tj
T*
(   While 20th-century scientific writing rigidly mandated passive voice across all manuscript) Tj
T*
(   sections, leading academic publishing houses \(Nature Portfolio, Science/AAAS, Cell Press, IEEE\)) Tj
T*
(   now explicitly encourage authors to deploy active voice where appropriate:) Tj
T*
(   - Nature Guidelines to Authors: "Nature journals prefer authors to write in the active voice) Tj
T*
(   \('we performed the experiment'\) rather than the passive \('the experiment was performed'\).") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rhetorical Environments Mandating Active Voice:) Tj
T*
(   - Introduction Section \(Establishing Research Aims\):) Tj
T*
(   - "In this study, we investigate the structural dynamics of CRISPR-Cas12a." \(Direct, energetic,) Tj
T*
(   assertive\).) Tj
T*
(   - Passive alternative is awkward and evasive: "In this study, the structural dynamics of) Tj
T*
(   CRISPR-Cas12a are investigated.") Tj
T*
(   - Highlighting Intellectual Agency and Unique Theoretical Choices:) Tj
T*
(   - When authors make a deliberate interpretive choice among competing methods:) Tj
T*
(   - "Because commercial kits produced low yields, we developed a customized phenol-chloroform) Tj
T*
(   protocol.") Tj
T*
(   - Eliminating Dangerous Ambiguity:) Tj
T*
(   - "Previous studies suggested that the protein forms dimers. Here, we demonstrate that it) Tj
T*
(   functions as a monomer." \(Clearly delineates historical consensus from current original) Tj
T*
(   findings\).) Tj
T*
(   - Discussion / Concluding Sections \(Formulating Hypotheses\):) Tj
T*
(   - "We propose a novel regulatory feedback model...") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze impersonal passive constructions \('It is reported that...', 'It was observed that...'\) and evaluate their stylistic impact.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Syntactic Architecture of Impersonal Passives:) Tj
T*
(   An impersonal passive pairs an expletive \(dummy\) pronoun 'it' with a passive reporting verb) Tj
T*
(   followed by a finite 'that'-clause acting as the extraposed subject:) Tj
T*
(   - Formula: It + [be + V3 of reporting verb] + that + [Proposition].) Tj
T*
(   - Examples: "It has been demonstrated that...", "It was found that...", "It is hypothesized) Tj
T*
(   that...".) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rhetorical Functions:) Tj
T*
(   - Institutional and Epistemic Neutrality: Allows the writer to articulate a finding or) Tj
T*
(   hypothesis as a matter of broad scientific observation without tethering it to a specific) Tj
T*
(   investigator:) Tj
T*
(   - "It is widely accepted that retroviruses reverse-transcribe RNA into DNA.") Tj
T*
(   - Prudent Academic Hedging: Cushions controversial or preliminary conclusions:) Tj
T*
(   - "It may be inferred that off-target cleavage was negligible.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Stylistic Hazards \(Wordiness and Throat-Clearing\):) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
